new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9ccbc6d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SPEC.md
@@ -0,0 +1,154 @@
+# Spec: mid-cycle plan changes
+
+## Why
+
+Customers cannot change plan today; support cancels and resubscribes them by hand. The
+billing package needs a self-serve plan change covering upgrades, downgrades and switches
+between monthly and annual billing. Changes must be prorated so that nobody pays twice
+for the same days. We never refund unused time.
+
+## Interface (fixed)
+
+- `BillingService.change_plan(subscription_id: str, new_plan_code: str, new_interval: Interval | None = None) -> Invoice | None`
+  in `src/billing/service.py`. `new_interval=None` keeps the subscription's current interval.
+- Returns the invoice issued for the change, recorded in the store like every other
+  invoice. Returns `None` when nothing is billed at the moment of the request.
+- `InvalidPlanChange(BillingError)` in `src/billing/errors.py` for change requests that
+  can't be honoured. The existing error classes are still used where they fit.
+
+## Terms
+
+- **Change date**: `clock.today()` at the time of the request.
+- **Current plan / current interval**: what the subscription is on now. A pending change
+  does not count as current.
+- **Requested plan / interval**: `new_plan_code`, and `new_interval` (or the current
+  interval when `new_interval` is `None`).
+- **Upgrade**: the requested plan's `monthly_price` is strictly greater than the current
+  plan's `monthly_price`, whichever interval the subscription is on. Every other plan
+  change is a **downgrade** for the purposes of this spec, including a different plan
+  with an equal monthly price.
+- **Remaining days**: the days from the change date (inclusive) to `period_end`
+  (exclusive).
+- **Period days**: the actual number of days in the current period, `period_end -
+  period_start` (28–31 for a monthly period, 365 or 366 for an annual one).
+- **Pending change**: a plan and/or interval that the subscription will move to at its
+  next renewal. A subscription has at most one pending change.
+
+## Behaviour
+
+### Active subscriptions
+
+| Request | Effect now | Effect at the next renewal |
+|---|---|---|
+| Upgrade, same interval | Plan switches now; proration invoice issued and returned | Bills the new plan in full |
+| Upgrade + interval switch | Plan switches now; proration invoice at the **current** interval's prices; interval switch becomes pending | New interval starts; bills the new plan at the new interval's full price |
+| Downgrade (with or without interval switch) | Nothing changes or is billed; change becomes pending; returns `None` | Moves to the requested plan and interval; bills its full price |
+| Interval switch only (same plan) | Nothing changes or is billed; becomes pending; returns `None` | New interval starts; bills the plan at that interval's full price |
+| Current plan and current interval, with a pending change | Pending change is cancelled; returns `None` | Renews unchanged |
+| Current plan and current interval, nothing pending | Raises `InvalidPlanChange` | — |
+
+The proration invoice for an upgrade:
+
+- is dated on the change date and has the subscription's id and customer id;
+- has exactly two lines:
+  1. a credit for the unused old plan: amount = −round(old plan price × remaining days ÷ period days);
+  2. a charge for the new plan over the same days: amount = +round(new plan price × remaining days ÷ period days);
+- uses the prices of the subscription's **current** interval for both lines;
+- computes each line exactly and then rounds it on its own to cents, half up (the
+  package's `to_money`). The invoice total is the sum of the two rounded lines;
+- is always issued, even when its total is negative (for example, when the new plan has
+  a higher monthly price but a lower annual price on an annual subscription). If the
+  total is exactly 0.00, the invoice may or may not be recorded, but the return value
+  must match: the recorded invoice, or `None` if nothing was recorded.
+
+### Trialing subscriptions
+
+Any change (upgrade, downgrade, interval switch, or a combination) applies immediately
+and in full. Nothing is billed, the method returns `None`, and nothing is left pending.
+The trial end date does not move. When the trial ends, the first paid period bills the
+full price of the plan and interval the subscription is on at that point.
+
+### Pending changes
+
+- A new request replaces any pending change.
+- An upgrade that applies now discards whatever was pending. If the same request also
+  switches interval, that interval switch becomes the new pending change.
+- The pending change has not happened yet. Upgrades and downgrades are judged against the
+  current plan, and proration credits the current plan. Example: on Pro with Basic
+  pending, upgrading to Premium credits Pro and charges Premium.
+- When renewal catches up several overdue periods at once, the pending change applies at
+  the first of them. That renewal and every later one bill the new plan and interval at
+  full price, with each period's length following the new interval.
+- Once applied at renewal, a pending change is cleared.
+
+### Rejections
+
+| Situation | Error |
+|---|---|
+| Subscription id unknown | `SubscriptionNotFound` |
+| Subscription canceled | `SubscriptionNotActive` |
+| `new_plan_code` unknown | `PlanNotFound` |
+| Requested plan is retired and is not the current plan | `PlanNotAvailable` |
+| Requested plan and interval equal the current ones and nothing is pending | `InvalidPlanChange` |
+| Subscription is overdue (`period_end <= change date`; renewals not yet run) | `InvalidPlanChange` |
+
+A customer on a retired plan may switch interval while staying on it, and may move off it
+like anyone else. A rejected request changes nothing: no subscription update, no
+invoice, and any pending change is left as it was.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+1. `InvalidPlanChange` exists in `billing.errors`, subclasses `BillingError`, and is
+   exported from the `billing` package like the other errors.
+2. Pro monthly 30.00 → Premium monthly 50.00, period `[2026-01-10, 2026-02-10)` (31
+   days), changed on 2026-01-25 (16 remaining days): the returned invoice is dated
+   2026-01-25, has exactly the lines −15.48 and +25.81, totals 10.33, and is the last
+   invoice in `store.invoices_for(subscription_id)`.
+3. After an upgrade, the subscription's `plan_code` is the new plan, and `period_start`,
+   `period_end`, `interval` and `status` are unchanged. The next renewal bills the new
+   plan's full price for the interval.
+4. An upgrade on the first day of a period credits the full old price and charges the
+   full new price.
+5. On an annual subscription, an upgrade uses annual prices and divides by 365 or 366
+   according to the actual period length.
+6. An upgrade where the new plan's annual price is below the old one's, on an annual
+   subscription, still issues the two-line invoice with a negative total.
+7. A downgrade returns `None`, records no invoice, and leaves `plan_code`, `interval` and
+   period dates unchanged. The next renewal bills the cheaper plan's full price.
+8. A different plan with an equal monthly price behaves as a downgrade (criterion 7).
+9. An interval-only switch, in either direction, returns `None` and records no invoice. The
+   next renewal starts on the old `period_end`, ends one period of the new interval
+   later, and bills the plan's full price for the new interval.
+10. Upgrade + interval switch: one proration invoice now at the current interval's prices
+    (as in 2). The next renewal starts a period of the new interval and bills the new
+    plan's full price for that interval.
+11. Downgrade + switch to annual: `None` now; the next renewal bills the cheaper plan's
+    full annual price for a 12-month period.
+12. Requesting the current plan and interval while a change is pending returns `None`, and
+    the next renewal is unchanged. With nothing pending it raises `InvalidPlanChange`.
+13. A second downgrade request replaces the first. Only the latest one applies at renewal.
+14. On Pro with Basic pending, upgrading to Premium credits Pro (not Basic) and charges
+    Premium. The next renewal bills Premium, not Basic.
+15. On a trial, any change returns `None`, records no invoice, and updates `plan_code` and
+    `interval` immediately. `period_end` (trial end) is unchanged, and the renewal at trial
+    end bills the full price of the new plan and interval.
+16. Each row of the rejections table raises the listed error, and afterwards the
+    subscription, its pending change and its invoices are exactly as before.
+17. A customer on a retired plan can switch interval on that plan, and can upgrade or
+    downgrade to an active plan.
+18. With overdue periods and a pending change, a single `renew_due` applies the change at
+    the first overdue renewal, and every invoice it issues bills the new plan and interval.
+19. Existing behaviour (`subscribe`, `renew_due`, `cancel`) and the existing test suite are
+    unchanged when no plan change is requested.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- Refunds, credit notes, or a customer credit balance. Downgrades and interval switches
+  never produce a credit.
+- Proration of downgrades or interval switches.
+- Changing the billing anchor: period dates never move because of a plan change.
+- Scheduling a change for an arbitrary future date. The only deferred moment is the next
+  renewal.
+- Charging or collecting payment. Invoices are recorded, as today.
+- Changes to plan pricing, plan retirement, or trial length.
+- Undoing an upgrade that has already been applied.
